===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# Of, relating to, or resembling [[rubber]], especially in consistency.
#: {{ux|en|What a bad restaurant! The beef was so '''rubbery''' I thought I'd never finish chewing it.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Harold McGee|title=Curious Cook; Why the Rubber Chicken Leg Can Bounce Across the Road|magazine=w:The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/1998/04/29/dining/curious-cook-why-the-rubber-chicken-leg-can-bounce-across-the-road.html|date=29-04-1988|passage=In this same temperature range, however, the leg is at its '''rubberiest'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Randall Munroe|title=Can You Boil an Egg Too Long?|magazine=w:The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/09/science/randall-munroe-question-eggs.html|date=09-06-2020|passage=If you boil it for hours, it becomes '''rubbery''' and overcooked.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Mike Edwards|title=Collaboration leads to eco-friendly straw made with polyhydroxyalkanoate|magazine=CPECN|url=https://www.cpecn.com/features/collaboration-leads-to-eco-friendly-straw-made-with-polyhydroxyalkanoate/|date=29-06-2023|passage=CJ Biomaterials was the first company in the world to produce amorphous PHA, it says, which is a softer, '''rubberier''' version of PHA that offers fundamentally different performance characteristics than crystalline or semi-crystalline forms of the biopolymer.}}

